# Nissan Juke F16 five-door crossover, 2019-.
#
# The second-generation Juke: taller, roomier and more upright than the F15, with
# larger squared lamp signature and a horizontal rear lamp cluster in place of
# the F15's hooked units.
# https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Nissan_Juke
#
# Dimensions 4.210 x 1.800 x 1.595 m, wheelbase 2.636 m, from the English
# Wikipedia F16 dimension box. Mirrors take the modelled width to 2.020 m.
#
# Colours. No UK colour chart for the F16 was located, so the objects carry plain
# colour names: white, red, black and grey. Weights white 3, red 3, black 2,
# grey 2, total 10, provisional pending the central rebase.
#
# Speed 190 km/h for the 1.0 DIG-T, the volume model. Comfort 95/320, on the line
# 180 + 1.5 x 95, two steps above the F15's 85/310 because the F16 is longer,
# wider and much roomier inside. Classes 1,2.
#
# Dates are road presence: November 2019 intro, retires staggered 2034-2037 on a
# fifteen- to eighteen-year tail.
#
# Metres master: citycars/4.5/nissan-juke-f16.blend. Interchange:
# citycars/4.5/nissan-juke-f16.dae (46 objects). References:
# citycars/references/nissan-juke-f16/ (gitignored; Wikimedia Commons).
#
# Accepted deviations: the rear lamps are smaller than the photographs and the
# bumper is simplified. At 128 px the upright hatch, the V grille and the
# horizontal rear lamps read as the F16.

obj=citycar
name=NissanJukeF16(White)
copyright=JamesPetts

DistributionWeight=3
intro_year=2019
intro_month=11
retire_year=2037
retire_month=6
speed=190
class=1,2
maximum_comfortable_journey_minutes=95
maximum_tolerable_journey_minutes=320

